CORE
main.c
--unwind 2 --rounds 2 --por --allow-pointer-unsoundness --slice-formula --verbosity 9
^EXIT=0$
^SIGNAL=0$
^thread-aware slicing removed [1-9][0-9]* assignments$
^VERIFICATION SUCCESSFUL$
--
^warning: ignoring
--
The slicer has to fire here (hence the "removed" line: a slicer that gives up
would pass the verdict check for the wrong reason) and it has to keep the
assignments feeding a shared write, which no step in the writing thread reads.
